{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00985",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 1.12,
      "end_seconds": 14.64,
      "duration_seconds": 13.52,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I'm Beth, I care for Mr Calloway during the day. He's been coughing at meals, and he's frightened to eat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.44,
      "end_seconds": 23.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "Thanks, Beth. Mr Calloway, can you tell me about it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.75,
      "end_seconds": 34.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "It's, well, when I eat, or drink. It goes down the wrong way, and I cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 37.06,
      "end_seconds": 42.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Every meal, doctor. Even a cup of tea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.71,
      "end_seconds": 47.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Does it feel like food sticks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.62,
      "end_seconds": 56.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Sometimes, yes. In the throat, like it won't go down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.16,
      "end_seconds": 63.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "How's your voice after you've had a drink?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 65.25,
      "end_seconds": 70.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "It goes wet and gurgly. You can hear it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.26,
      "end_seconds": 75.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Any weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 78.19,
      "end_seconds": 84.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "No, not that I've noticed, we've been giving him milkshakes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.59,
      "end_seconds": 89.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Any chest infections recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.49,
      "end_seconds": 93.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "No. No chest infections."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.73,
      "end_seconds": 98.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "What medicines is he taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.92,
      "end_seconds": 107.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.72,
      "text": "Levothyroxine, 50 micrograms, every morning. And metoprolol, 25 mg, twice a day, I take both every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 109.08,
      "end_seconds": 118.31,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "It's 75 micrograms, Alf, the levothyroxine. And he forgets the evening metoprolol about three times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.88,
      "end_seconds": 123.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "I don't forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.68,
      "end_seconds": 130.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "We'll check the pharmacy about the levothyroxine. Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.8,
      "end_seconds": 135.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "None. No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.96,
      "end_seconds": 139.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.67,
      "end_seconds": 148.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.54,
      "text": "I had a stroke, two years ago. And the thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.05,
      "end_seconds": 151.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Any dementia in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 154.49,
      "end_seconds": 158.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "His mother had dementia, he told me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.73,
      "end_seconds": 164.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Who's at home with him?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 167.13,
      "end_seconds": 171.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "His wife, and I come in at meal times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.44,
      "end_seconds": 199.95,
      "duration_seconds": 10.51,
      "text": "Let me check your numbers. Pulse 74, blood pressure 138 over 82, temperature 36.7, oxygen 96 percent, breathing 16, weight 66 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 201.9,
      "end_seconds": 205.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Is that all right? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.7,
      "end_seconds": 213.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Noted. Any trouble with your breathing at rest, Mr Calloway?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.2,
      "end_seconds": 217.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "No, nothing at rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.95,
      "end_seconds": 229.3,
      "duration_seconds": 11.35,
      "text": "Here's what I think. The coughing at meals after a stroke, with the wet voice, suggests swallowing difficulty after the stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 231.92,
      "end_seconds": 234.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Is that common? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.43,
      "end_seconds": 250.04,
      "duration_seconds": 14.61,
      "text": "Very. I'm also concerned that some food or drink may go into the lungs, so I can't rule out that it's already getting there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.89,
      "end_seconds": 255.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Is that serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.34,
      "end_seconds": 267.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.66,
      "text": "It can be, which is why I'd like to arrange a swallowing assessment with a speech therapist, soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 268.52,
      "end_seconds": 272.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "When can he have it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.24,
      "end_seconds": 283.81,
      "duration_seconds": 8.57,
      "text": "Within the week. Meanwhile, give him smaller, softer mouthfuls, sit him fully upright, and no straws."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 286.74,
      "end_seconds": 289.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I'll do that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.63,
      "end_seconds": 301.98,
      "duration_seconds": 10.35,
      "text": "If he gets a fever, a new cough, or seems more breathless, ring us the same day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 303.3,
      "end_seconds": 306.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I will. Thank you, doctor. ~"
    }
  ]
}
